  "final_text": "## Result\n\nFor **W = 1.5929 GeV, Q\u00b2 = 0.4276 GeV\u00b2, cos \u03b8* = 0.651724, \u03c6* = 36\u00b0** (6.53 GeV beam, vcut = 0.166 GeV\u00b2, full O(\u03b1) unpolarized EtaMAID calculation):\n\n- **\u03b4 = 1.1413042153**\n- **\u03c3_Born = 0.0055907670**\n\n(values taken verbatim from `eta/radtot.dat`, full double precision, unpolarized structure functions)\n\nNote on process: `exclurad` hardcodes `open(unit=5,file='input.dat')` internally, so it ignores stdin redirection \u2014 I had to write the kinematic point directly into `eta/input.dat` (saved as `eta/my_input.dat` for the record) before running, then restored the original 3-point template file afterward. The integration diagnostics (`test : 0.559E-02 0.559E-02 1.00`) confirm the calculation converged cleanly, and W is safely above the ep\u2192e'p\u03b7 threshold (1.4861 GeV), so the point is physical.\n\nFull details are in `outcome.json`.",
